# Global agent rules

- **Output & ownership**: lead with the conclusion in the user's language, separate measured facts from inferences; implement, run targeted checks and wrap up autonomously, pausing only for the major decisions below.
${SUPERVISOR_RULE}
- **Workspace & isolation (`${WORKSPACE_ROOT}`)**: keep main clones in `Projects/<project>` on `main` (read their `AGENTS.md` when present); **One writer per directory** — edit code in an isolated worktree under `{Orca,Codex,Claude}/Worktrees/` (`${BRANCH_PREFIX}/<topic>`), never directly on main clones.
- **Temp folders**: project zones are `docs/`, `reports/<date-topic>/`, `outputs/<topic>/`, `work/`; allocate temp/test dirs and `-derivedDataPath` via `agent-governor scratch|test-dir --topic <topic>`, keeping roots clean.
${VOLUME_RULE}
- **Guardrails (`agent-guard`)**: destructive deletes, dangerous Git commands, force-pushes, restricted pushes and root clutter are blocked by `agent-guard` with safe alternatives — follow the hint and never bypass it; archive dirty worktrees to `Archive/` before moving to the Trash.${RESTRICTED_RULE}
- **Names & test devices**: name Orca workspaces, worktrees and tabs `Project｜Topic` (full-width bar, no spaces); run disposable iOS simulators and QEMU VMs via `agent-test-device` (cleanup and device details live in `orca-workspace` skill).
- **Shipping (`agent-ship`)**: once targeted checks pass, commit on the task branch and run `agent-ship`; use `agent-ship --no-merge` for **major decisions**: ① deleting/migrating user data or schemas; ② store submissions/releases; ③ signing, entitlements, accounts, billing or secrets; ④ breaking public interfaces or large cross-project refactors; ⑤ ambiguous conflicts or CI failing twice.
